      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a4",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1585097790,
      "version": 843,
      "versionNonce": 2113364258,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "TmZnXIU9_YbHtsrG5iS-k",
          "type": "arrow"
        },
        {
          "id": "hNvxWin14KImh_MU1QwsQ",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1793247137929,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Steps to create balance tree\n---------------------------------------\n\n1. Start creating the Tree just like BST .\n\n2. After adding each node check its balance factor .\n\n3. If BF is beyond -1, 0 or 1 then the node is considered as critical\nnode and the tree is not balanced .\n\n4. Before adding next node we have to make the tree balance .\n\n5. When tree is balanced only then we proceed to add the next node .\n\n\nHow to Balance the tree\n--------------------------------\n\n->    Rotation ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Steps to create balance tree\n---------------------------------------\n\n1. Start creating the Tree just like BST .\n\n2. After adding each node check its balance factor .\n\n3. If BF is beyond -1, 0 or 1 then the node is considered as critical node and the tree is not balanced .\n\n4. Before adding next node we have to make the tree balance .\n\n5. When tree is balanced only then we proceed to add the next node .\n\n\nHow to Balance the tree\n--------------------------------\n\n->    Rotation ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
